**{n}.1 Management.** The Company is manager-managed. {manager_name} is the Manager and, subject to Section {n}.2, has full authority to manage the business and affairs of the Company.

**{n}.2 Reserved Matters.** Notwithstanding Section {n}.1, the Company shall not, and the Manager shall not cause the Company to, take any of the following actions without the Approval of the Members:

(a) sell, transfer, or otherwise dispose of all or substantially all of the Company's assets, or any Property;

(b) incur, guarantee, refinance, or materially amend any indebtedness, or grant any lien or encumbrance over any Company asset;

(c) admit any new Member, or issue, redeem, or reclassify any Units;

(d) enter into, amend, or terminate any transaction with the Manager or any Affiliate of the Manager, or approve any compensation payable to them;

(e) change the purpose of the Company, or commence any business outside that purpose;

(f) make any distribution other than in accordance with this Agreement;

(g) commence, settle, or compromise any litigation involving an amount exceeding {litigation_threshold};

(h) approve or materially deviate from the annual budget;

(i) file for bankruptcy, dissolve, or wind up the Company; or

(j) amend this Agreement or the Certificate of Formation.

**{n}.3 Approval of the Members.** "Approval of the Members" means the written approval of Members holding at least {member_approval_threshold} of the Units, provided that any action under Section {n}.2(d) requires the approval of a majority of the Units held by Members other than the Manager and its Affiliates.

**{n}.4 Standard of Care.** The Manager shall discharge its duties in good faith, with the care an ordinarily prudent person in a like position would exercise, and in a manner it reasonably believes to be in the best interests of the Company.

**{n}.5 Removal.** The Manager may be removed for Cause by the Approval of the Members, excluding for this purpose any Units held by the Manager and its Affiliates. "Cause" means fraud, wilful misconduct, gross negligence, a material breach of this Agreement that remains uncured thirty (30) days after written notice, or a felony conviction relating to the business of the Company.
